      "title": "Core Modules and the fs Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Core Modules and the fs Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Core modules",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Core modules ship with Node: ==no install==",
                "Import with the ==node: prefix== to show they are built in",
                "`import fs from 'node:fs'`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Three fs API styles",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Style",
                "Call",
                "Event loop",
                "Errors"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Callback",
                  "`fs.readFile(path, cb)`",
                  "{green:free} (thread pool)",
                  "`cb(err, data)`"
                ],
                [
                  "Sync",
                  "`fs.readFileSync`",
                  "{red:blocked} until done",
                  "{red:throws}"
                ],
                [
                  "Promise",
                  "`fs/promises` or `fs.promises.readFile`",
                  "{green:free} (thread pool)",
                  "rejects"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Callback: ==err is always the first argument==",
                "Sync: wrap in `try/catch`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "import fs from 'node:fs';",
                "import { readFile } from 'node:fs/promises';",
                "fs.readFile('a.txt', 'utf8', (err, data) => {});",
                "const text = await readFile('a.txt', 'utf8');",
                "try { fs.readFileSync('a.txt', 'utf8'); } catch (e) {}"
              ],
              "note": "callback, promise, sync"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Buffer or string",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "No encoding → ==Buffer==",
                "Pass `'utf8'` → string"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Sync blocks everything",
              "text": "`readFileSync` freezes the **whole** event loop until it finishes."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "fs Workflow: Promises, Callbacks and Sync Compared",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "fs Workflow: Promises, Callbacks and Sync Compared",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Which Style",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Preferred: ==fs/promises== + `await` inside **try/catch**",
                "Import: `import { readFile, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises'`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Style",
                "Suits"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Callbacks",
                  "legacy code"
                ],
                [
                  "Sync",
                  "startup scripts, CLIs"
                ],
                [
                  "{green:Promises}",
                  "servers, everything else"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Writing and Everyday Calls",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Read, transform, write back, with errors caught"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "try {",
                "  const text = await readFile('a.txt', 'utf8');",
                "  await writeFile('b.txt', text.toUpperCase());",
                "} catch (err) {",
                "  console.error(err.message);",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`writeFile` ==overwrites==; `appendFile` **adds**",
                "Flag `'wx'` fails if the file ==exists==",
                "Everyday calls: mkdir, readdir, stat, rm, access"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "await mkdir(dir, { recursive: true });",
                "await readdir(dir);",
                "await stat(file);",
                "await access(file);",
                "await rm(p, { recursive: true, force: true });"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`readFileSync` in a request handler ==blocks every request==",
                "Missing `await` or `err` check: silent failure, unhandled rejection"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "path and __dirname in ES Modules",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "path and __dirname in ES Modules",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. join vs resolve",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`join` ==concatenates== segments and normalizes separators and `..`",
                "The result of `join` can stay ==relative==",
                "`resolve` builds an ==absolute== path, processing right to left until absolute",
                "If no segment is absolute, it falls back to `process.cwd()`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Call",
                "Result",
                "Why"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`join('/a', '/b')`",
                  "`/a/b`",
                  "just joins"
                ],
                [
                  "`resolve('/a', '/b')`",
                  "`/b`",
                  "absolute segment **resets**"
                ],
                [
                  "`join('a', '..', 'b')`",
                  "`b`",
                  "stays relative"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. __dirname in ESM",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`__dirname` and `__filename` exist in ==CommonJS only==",
                "Missing with `type: module` or `.mjs`",
                "Newer Node: `import.meta.dirname`, `import.meta.filename`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "import path from 'node:path';",
                "import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';",
                "",
                "const __dirname = path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url));"
              ],
              "note": "the ESM replacement"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Helpers and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`basename`, `extname`, `dirname`, `parse` split a path",
                "Use ==path.sep==; never hard-code `/` or `\\`"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "The cwd trap",
              "text": "`'./data.json'` resolves against ==process.cwd()==, not the file. Anchor it: `path.join(__dirname, 'data.json')`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The http Module and a Minimal Server",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "The http Module and a Minimal Server",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Server, req and res",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`http.createServer(cb)` returns a ==server==; cb runs **once per request**",
                "`server.listen(port)` starts it",
                "`req`: ==readable stream== with `req.method`, `req.url`, `req.headers`",
                "`res`: ==writable stream**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "js",
              "lines": [
                "import { createServer } from 'node:http';",
                "createServer((req, res) => {",
                "  res.writeHead(200, { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' });",
                "  res.end(JSON.stringify({ ok: true }));",
                "}).listen(3000);"
              ],
              "note": "minimal JSON server"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Routing and Body",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Route by hand on method + pathname; ==Express== and ==Fastify== wrap this same API",
                "Body arrives in **chunks**: collect in `data`, parse in `end`",
                "Or: `for await (const c of req)`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "js",
              "lines": [
                "const url = new URL(req.url, 'http://localhost');",
                "if (req.method === 'GET' && url.pathname === '/health') {",
                "  return res.end('ok');",
                "}",
                "let body = '';",
                "req.on('data', c => body += c);",
                "req.on('end', () => JSON.parse(body));"
              ],
              "note": "inside the handler"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "No `res.end()`: the request ==hangs==",
                "`writeHead` or `setHeader` after the body is sent: {red:ERR_HTTP_HEADERS_SENT}",
                "No `Content-Type`, or an object passed to `res.end` (needs string or Buffer)"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
